    {
      "ability_id": "paladin_hammer_of_justice",
      "name": "Hammer of Justice",
      "resource_type": "mana",
      "cooldown": 5,
      "effect_type": "debuff",
      "duration": 2,
      "stat_mods": {},
      "description": "Stuns the target with a hammer of Light for 2 turns.",
      "ranks": [
        {
          "rank": 1,
          "level_req": 8,
          "cost": 35,
          "effect_value": 43
        },
        {
          "rank": 2,
          "level_req": 24,
          "cost": 53,
          "effect_value": 71
        },
        {
          "rank": 3,
          "level_req": 44,
          "cost": 71,
          "effect_value": 100
        }
      ],
      "icon_id": null,
      "buff_scope": "combat",
      "is_stun": true,
      "_source": "  DID NOT STUN. Its description is 'Stuns the target with a hammer of Light for 2 turns' and it carried no is_stun - just haste -25 and attack_power -30 standing in for the stun, so the player read 'stuns' and got a slow. The stun mechanic is live end to end (StatusEffect.is_stun -> StatusEffectMixin.is_stunned -> turn_meter skips the turn) and Paladin already has two real stuns in Repentance (2 turns / 5 cd) and Turn Evil (2/6). Matched to Repentance's 5-turn cooldown, up from 4, because a 2-turn hard stun on a 4-turn cooldown is half the fight. The haste/AP stand-in is removed - a stunned target cannot act at all, so debuffing its haste for the same two turns is dead weight."
    },
